1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:03:39,575 --> 00:03:41,406
Look out, Mr. Potato Head!

3
00:03:58,027 --> 00:03:59,426
Good morning, Speck!

4
00:04:02,098 --> 00:04:05,261
Me, too. Come on.
Let's get some breakfast.

5
00:05:09,465 --> 00:05:10,864
Mad dog!

6
00:06:49,432 --> 00:06:50,831
Good morning, Pee-wee.

7
00:06:51,267 --> 00:06:53,292
Good morning, Mr. Breakfast.

8
00:06:54,437 --> 00:06:56,769
Can I have my "Mr. T" cereal?

9
00:06:59,642 --> 00:07:03,043
I pity the poor fool
who don't eat my cereal!

10
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:34,977
Here, Speck.

11
00:07:36,913 --> 00:07:38,346
Welp, I'm off.

12
00:07:39,182 --> 00:07:40,342
You be good.

13
00:07:59,135 --> 00:08:00,932
Good morning, Mr. Crabtree.

14
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:02,432
Good morning, Pee-wee.

15
00:08:02,672 --> 00:08:04,503
I'm going to water my lawn.

16
00:09:05,068 --> 00:09:07,935
Good morning. I'm here.

17
00:09:33,362 --> 00:09:35,956
You're the best bike in the whole world.

18
00:09:46,976 --> 00:09:49,035
Brush-brush-brush.
Brush-brush-brush.

19
00:11:29,036 --> 00:11:30,025
I meant to do that.

20
00:12:54,355 --> 00:12:55,720
My good friend, Pee-wee!

21
00:12:56,023 --> 00:12:57,354
Hi, Mario.

22
00:12:57,825 --> 00:12:59,520
Are you just browsing today?

23
00:13:00,361 --> 00:13:02,852
Sort of. I wanted to stock up
on some supplies.

24
00:13:03,664 --> 00:13:04,528
Help yourself.

25
00:13:10,438 --> 00:13:11,735
How do you like school?

26
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,366
Closed.

27
00:13:23,284 --> 00:13:24,876
What?

28
00:13:38,866 --> 00:13:41,391
I got some new items
you might be interested in.

29
00:13:52,914 --> 00:13:55,280
Box for Pee-wee.

30
00:13:56,651 --> 00:13:59,085
New, improved, squirting flower.

31
00:14:01,822 --> 00:14:03,414
Fake blood, or is it?

32
00:14:05,259 --> 00:14:06,419
Super stink-bomb?

33
00:14:06,994 --> 00:14:07,926
Have some.

34
00:14:08,296 --> 00:14:09,422
Shrunken head?

35
00:14:12,166 --> 00:14:13,098
Regular size?

36
00:14:21,242 --> 00:14:22,106
Trick gum?

37
00:14:25,012 --> 00:14:26,104
Headlight glasses?

38
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:32,818
And direct from Australia,
The Boomerang Bow-Tie!

39
00:14:33,988 --> 00:14:34,886
Come in red?

40
00:14:48,703 --> 00:14:50,136
I'll be right back.

41
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,083
-What's up, man?
-How's it going?

42
00:15:08,422 --> 00:15:10,413
Is Dottie still working on your bike?

43
00:15:10,658 --> 00:15:12,649
No, I've got it back already.

44
00:15:13,361 --> 00:15:14,350
What's she doing to it?

45
00:15:14,829 --> 00:15:18,492
I can't talk about it.
James Bond kind of stuff.

46
00:15:19,967 --> 00:15:21,491
Dottie's radical with bikes.

47
00:15:23,437 --> 00:15:24,995
I say we cruise, dudes.

48
00:15:25,906 --> 00:15:26,998
It's getting hot in here.

49
00:15:27,608 --> 00:15:28,666
It's steamy.

50
00:15:29,310 --> 00:15:30,436
I'm sweating.

51
00:15:33,681 --> 00:15:35,012
Is my horn ready yet?

52
00:15:35,616 --> 00:15:38,176
It's ready. It should be
loud enough for you now.

53
00:15:38,953 --> 00:15:40,511
Where is it? Let's hear it.

54
00:15:45,693 --> 00:15:47,354
Wait. I want to talk to you first.

55
00:15:47,561 --> 00:15:49,188
You are talking to me.

56
00:15:49,563 --> 00:15:51,554
No, I want your undivided attention.

57
00:15:53,067 --> 00:15:55,695
This is important.
I want to ask you something.

58
00:16:01,075 --> 00:16:03,043
I want to know,
if you will do something?

59
00:16:04,078 --> 00:16:05,375
What?

60
00:16:06,213 --> 00:16:09,580
I want to know if you'll
go someplace with me.

61
00:16:09,884 --> 00:16:11,579
Like where?

62
00:16:13,587 --> 00:16:14,713
The drive-in.

63
00:16:17,091 --> 00:16:18,922
Look, Dottie, I like you.

64
00:16:19,627 --> 00:16:20,958
Like! I like you.

65
00:16:21,162 --> 00:16:22,720
I like you, too.

66
00:16:24,565 --> 00:16:27,227
There are a lot of things about me
you don't know anything about.

67
00:16:27,601 --> 00:16:31,594
Things you wouldn't understand,
you couldn't understand.

68
00:16:31,906 --> 00:16:34,739
Things you shouldn't understand.

69
00:16:35,609 --> 00:16:37,406
I don't understand.

70
00:16:37,845 --> 00:16:40,336
You don't want to get mixed up with me.

71
00:16:41,115 --> 00:16:43,913
I'm a Ioner, Dottie. A rebel.

72
00:16:48,622 --> 00:16:49,919
So long, Dot.

73
00:17:47,481 --> 00:17:48,573
Are you the owner?

74
00:17:48,816 --> 00:17:52,308
Yes. That's me. They call me Chuck.

75
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:54,251
Can I do anything?

76
00:17:54,588 --> 00:17:56,249
We're losing time!

77
00:17:56,590 --> 00:17:59,684
Set up a dragnet!
Comb the whole area! Hurry!

78
00:18:00,861 --> 00:18:04,262
I'm afraid we can't consider your bike
being stolen a police emergency.

79
00:18:04,331 --> 00:18:07,698
If it doesn't turn up, come to
the station and fill out a report.

80
00:18:08,002 --> 00:18:10,493
That's the best we can do.
Come on, let's go.

81
00:18:14,208 --> 00:18:15,505
Where are you going?

82
00:18:15,843 --> 00:18:17,504
To find my bike!

83
00:19:39,193 --> 00:19:42,526
Why exactly do you believe
the Soviets were involved?

84
00:19:44,365 --> 00:19:49,029
Let me be honest. Hundreds of bikes
are stolen every month.

85
00:19:49,370 --> 00:19:52,862
Very few of them are recovered.
We don't have the resources.

86
00:19:53,207 --> 00:19:55,573
You're saying you can't do anything.

87
00:19:55,976 --> 00:19:58,035
My bike means everything to me.

88
00:19:58,812 --> 00:20:00,643
I knew the police wouldn't help.

89
00:20:01,048 --> 00:20:03,039
You know what I'd do?

90
00:20:04,551 --> 00:20:06,542
Retrace my steps.

91
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:09,789
I parked my bike and
when I came back it was gone.

92
00:20:10,224 --> 00:20:13,057
Can you think of anyone
who'd want to take it?

93
00:20:13,394 --> 00:20:15,225
Everyone wanted my bike.

94
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,420
Cash only.

95
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:18,247
No cards, no checks.

96
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:19,422
You got cash?

97
00:20:23,797 --> 00:20:25,424
Let me take your jacket.

98
00:20:26,533 --> 00:20:30,264
You want to wear a wet jacket,
it's all right with Madam Ruby.

99
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:38,104
For $20 I can tell you a lot of things.
For $30 I can tell you more.

100
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:41,437
And for $50 I can tell you everything.

101
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:43,181
Tell me why I'm here.

102
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:46,442
You're here because you...

103
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,111
...want something.

104
00:20:58,298 --> 00:20:59,629
Let's see...

105
00:21:00,534 --> 00:21:02,798
...what Madam Ruby sees.

106
00:21:08,375 --> 00:21:10,138
I see...

107
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:11,637
...a bicycle.

108
00:21:11,912 --> 00:21:14,403
Yes! Is it okay?

109
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:15,945
It's okay.

110
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:19,145
Where is it?! Can you see it?
Where is it?!

111
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:22,482
Where is it?

112
00:21:24,091 --> 00:21:26,924
It's somewhere else.
Somewhere far away.

113
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:28,225
Where?!

114
00:21:38,172 --> 00:21:39,230
The Alamo.

115
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:44,166
The Alamo.

116
00:21:48,949 --> 00:21:50,678
In the basement.

117
00:21:53,053 --> 00:21:54,577
I'll never forget you.

118
00:22:56,450 --> 00:22:59,419
Thanks a million.
I've been trying all day.

119
00:23:07,361 --> 00:23:09,591
-The name's Mickey.
-I'm Pee-wee.

120
00:23:17,404 --> 00:23:18,268
How about some music?

121
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:21,373
Morelli is armed and dangerous...

122
00:23:21,742 --> 00:23:23,107
Forget the music.

123
00:23:23,644 --> 00:23:25,271
Let's enjoy the scenery.

124
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:33,051
What did you do?

125
00:23:39,026 --> 00:23:41,290
I lost my temper, took a knife
and I...

126
00:23:44,097 --> 00:23:48,124
You know those "Do not remove under
penalty of law" labels on mattresses?

127
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:51,627
I cut one off.

128
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:56,802
I got a real bad temper.

129
00:23:57,444 --> 00:23:59,810
I always thought that was a dumb law.

130
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:01,138
You said a mouthful.

131
00:24:02,716 --> 00:24:04,479
Life can be so unfair.

132
00:24:05,619 --> 00:24:06,517
You're telling me?!

133
00:24:57,704 --> 00:25:01,538
I tried to go through legal channels.
But the cops, hah!

134
00:25:02,009 --> 00:25:05,035
They were no help.
They gave me the runaround.

135
00:25:06,246 --> 00:25:09,374
That's when I decided to take
the law into my own hands.

136
00:25:09,850 --> 00:25:10,714
The law...

137
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:13,049
The law.

138
00:25:13,387 --> 00:25:14,547
The law.

139
00:25:15,856 --> 00:25:16,515
The law!

140
00:25:18,825 --> 00:25:19,689
This is it.

141
00:25:21,662 --> 00:25:23,061
I got an idea!

142
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,400
What's going on?

143
00:25:34,741 --> 00:25:36,902
We're looking for an escaped convict.

144
00:25:37,244 --> 00:25:40,907
We heard about it on the radio.
Right, honey?

145
00:25:41,982 --> 00:25:43,176
Have you seen this man?

146
00:25:45,752 --> 00:25:48,084
I've seen better heads on boils!

147
00:25:49,289 --> 00:25:52,087
No, I'm sure I'd remember this face.

148
00:25:56,363 --> 00:25:59,924
-Would you mind stepping out of the car.
-No, not at all, officer.

149
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,966
-Some sort of problem?
-Not at all.

150
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:05,936
I wanted to look at
that cute outfit you have on.

151
00:26:10,510 --> 00:26:13,104
Why don't you take a picture?
It'll last longer.

152
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,621
You have a nice day.

153
00:27:06,032 --> 00:27:08,432
What's it like in the big house, Mickey?

154
00:27:09,903 --> 00:27:11,495
It's not so bad.

155
00:27:12,439 --> 00:27:15,840
You get to lift weights,
watch TV, write up appeals...

156
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:18,838
...take long showers, lift weights.

157
00:27:20,647 --> 00:27:22,171
You get used to it.

158
00:28:30,851 --> 00:28:31,749
Out!

159
00:28:32,152 --> 00:28:33,346
Out!

160
00:28:34,888 --> 00:28:36,150
It wasn't my fault.

161
00:28:36,423 --> 00:28:39,586
Look kid, I like you. I like you a lot.

162
00:28:39,926 --> 00:28:41,917
That's why I can't drag you into this.

163
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:45,595
I'm bad. You don't get mixed up
with a guy like me.

164
00:28:45,932 --> 00:28:47,957
I'm a Ioner. A rebel!

165
00:28:49,503 --> 00:28:50,765
D�j� vu.

166
00:28:51,004 --> 00:28:52,972
See you in the Promised Land.

167
00:28:53,206 --> 00:28:55,003
Arrivederci, baby!

168
00:29:00,347 --> 00:29:01,314
Wait!

169
00:29:04,284 --> 00:29:06,775
I'm in the middle of nowhere!

170
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:14,449
Sure is spooky out here.

171
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:31,307
Probably just a dog.

172
00:29:42,222 --> 00:29:43,484
Kitty.

173
00:29:50,297 --> 00:29:52,663
Where's those headlight glasses?

174
00:30:27,340 --> 00:30:31,897
Welcome to the San Antonio Department
of Parks and Recreation Alamo tour.

175
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:34,001
My name is Tina.

176
00:30:34,308 --> 00:30:36,538
Excuse me Tina,
but could we go straight...

177
00:30:36,844 --> 00:30:40,075
Let's hold all questions
until the end of the tour.

178
00:30:41,249 --> 00:30:42,477
Thank you.

179
00:30:43,418 --> 00:30:47,081
This Mission, the Alamo, named from
the Spanish word for cottonwood tree...

180
00:30:47,321 --> 00:30:50,256
...was established in the year 1718.

181
00:30:50,658 --> 00:30:55,254
The same year that our city was founded
by the Spanish expeditionary force...

182
00:30:55,496 --> 00:30:58,431
...on the site of
an Indian burial mound.

183
00:30:58,733 --> 00:31:01,759
This is one of my favorite parts
of the tour.

184
00:31:01,869 --> 00:31:06,033
Please say hello to our residents,
Pedro and his wife, Inez.

185
00:31:06,407 --> 00:31:09,672
Inez is holding a clay pot
that she seems very proud of.

186
00:31:10,011 --> 00:31:13,674
She carefully detailed it
with paint and glaze.

187
00:31:14,582 --> 00:31:16,948
And Pedro is working on an "adobe."

188
00:31:17,185 --> 00:31:20,177
Can you say that with me? Adobe.

189
00:31:23,691 --> 00:31:26,455
We are now in the kitchen
of the Alamo women.

190
00:31:26,861 --> 00:31:30,353
Here they are preparing
culinary delights of the Southwest.

191
00:31:30,698 --> 00:31:32,689
Do I hear someone's stomach growling?

192
00:31:35,036 --> 00:31:37,698
The mainstay of the Alamo diet is corn.

193
00:31:38,039 --> 00:31:40,030
Corn can be prepared many ways.

194
00:31:40,374 --> 00:31:43,537
It can be boiled, shucked,
creamed...

195
00:31:43,811 --> 00:31:45,642
...or in this case dried.

196
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:48,271
Corn can also be used to make...

197
00:31:48,950 --> 00:31:49,644
...tortillas.

198
00:31:50,485 --> 00:31:53,386
Do we have any Mexican-Americans
with us today?

199
00:31:58,126 --> 00:32:01,391
There are thousands and thousands
of uses for corn...

200
00:32:01,729 --> 00:32:04,391
...all of which I will
tell you about right now.

201
00:32:04,899 --> 00:32:07,390
Upon this battlement, in 1836...

202
00:32:07,735 --> 00:32:09,396
...two hundred Texas volunteers...

203
00:32:09,737 --> 00:32:13,901
...including such heroes as
Davy Crockett, Bill Travis, Jim Bowie...

204
00:32:14,242 --> 00:32:17,405
...fought off an onslaught
of 4,000 Mexicans...

205
00:32:17,578 --> 00:32:21,412
...under the command of
General Antonio Lopez de Santa Ana.

206
00:32:23,551 --> 00:32:25,781
At this time, I'd like
to conclude our tour.

207
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:29,981
You all have been one of the greatest
groups I have ever worked with.

208
00:32:30,758 --> 00:32:32,589
Are there any questions?

209
00:32:34,195 --> 00:32:35,423
Where's the basement?

210
00:32:36,764 --> 00:32:38,595
Aren't we going to see the basement?

211
00:32:39,767 --> 00:32:42,099
There's no basement at the Alamo.

212
00:33:30,484 --> 00:33:33,009
Pee-wee, I'm on my way to Paris.

213
00:33:33,821 --> 00:33:36,312
Andy and I had a fight after you left.

214
00:33:36,657 --> 00:33:38,215
You were right, Pee-wee.

215
00:33:38,292 --> 00:33:40,522
I'm making my wish come true.

216
00:33:40,995 --> 00:33:43,486
I'm off to Paris!

217
00:33:47,268 --> 00:33:47,996
What's wrong?

218
00:33:48,236 --> 00:33:51,262
Bus 91, leaving for New York City,
now departing.

219
00:33:51,339 --> 00:33:53,000
That's my bus.

220
00:33:54,709 --> 00:33:55,903
Come on.

221
00:33:56,377 --> 00:34:00,006
Guess what. The Alamo was built
without a basement.

222
00:34:00,348 --> 00:34:01,679
I didn't know that.

223
00:34:01,816 --> 00:34:05,343
Neither did I. They don't tell you
that stuff in school.

224
00:34:05,686 --> 00:34:08,519
It's something you
just have to experience.

225
00:34:11,359 --> 00:34:14,692
Don't worry, Pee-wee.
I know you'll find your bike.

226
00:34:28,042 --> 00:34:31,569
Good luck. I just know
you're going to find your bike.

227
00:34:56,237 --> 00:34:58,569
Hello, Dottie? It's me, Pee-wee.

228
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:00,571
Where are you calling from?

229
00:35:00,908 --> 00:35:02,239
Texas.

230
00:35:03,144 --> 00:35:05,237
Honest. Listen, I'll prove it.

231
00:35:05,880 --> 00:35:09,407
"The stars at night
Are big and bright...

232
00:35:09,917 --> 00:35:12,909
"Deep in the heart of Texas."

233
00:35:13,587 --> 00:35:16,147
Wait. Don't hang up.
There's something...

234
00:35:16,223 --> 00:35:18,418
...I have to talk to you about.

235
00:35:19,493 --> 00:35:21,256
It's about the other night.

236
00:35:22,530 --> 00:35:26,364
I owe everybody a big apology.
Especially you.

237
00:35:27,768 --> 00:35:30,931
I didn't mean what I said, Dottie.
Honest.

238
00:35:31,272 --> 00:35:32,899
I know you didn't.

239
00:35:33,074 --> 00:35:35,542
There's somebody else
who's been worried about you.

240
00:35:42,116 --> 00:35:44,016
I know.

241
00:35:44,919 --> 00:35:46,011
I forgot.

242
00:35:48,622 --> 00:35:49,953
All right, Speck!

243
00:35:52,626 --> 00:35:55,459
All right, Speck! Put Dottie back on.

244
00:36:00,468 --> 00:36:02,629
There's something I want to say.

245
00:36:04,372 --> 00:36:07,307
I've learned something
out here on the road.

246
00:36:08,175 --> 00:36:08,971
Humility.

247
00:36:12,146 --> 00:36:16,310
Dottie, when I get back,
will you...

248
00:36:16,884 --> 00:36:17,816
What, Pee-wee?

249
00:36:19,687 --> 00:36:21,484
Will you still help me find my bike?

250
00:36:24,592 --> 00:36:25,650
All right.

251
00:36:26,394 --> 00:36:28,828
There's something else
I wanted to ask you about.

252
00:36:29,397 --> 00:36:30,329
What is it?

253
00:36:31,699 --> 00:36:34,998
Could you wire me a bus ticket?
I'll pay you back. Honest.

254
00:36:35,336 --> 00:36:37,201
All right, Pee-wee.

255
00:36:37,271 --> 00:36:40,331
When you get back,
we can settle up at the drive-in.

256
00:36:40,408 --> 00:36:41,466
What?

257
00:36:44,412 --> 00:36:46,437
I couldn't hear that last part.

258
00:36:46,514 --> 00:36:48,914
The connection just got really bad.

259
00:36:49,417 --> 00:36:50,748
Thanks a lot.

260
00:36:59,427 --> 00:37:00,758
What's your name?

261
00:37:01,262 --> 00:37:03,253
I can't remember.

262
00:37:03,698 --> 00:37:05,063
Where you from?

263
00:37:05,700 --> 00:37:07,531
I can't remember.

264
00:37:07,668 --> 00:37:09,329
Can't you remember anything?

265
00:37:10,504 --> 00:37:12,995
I remember the Alamo.

266
00:37:45,039 --> 00:37:47,872
I'm sorry, operator. I can't hear you.

267
00:37:51,045 --> 00:37:54,037
I'm trying to use the phone!

268
00:38:03,331 --> 00:38:04,662
Why not?

269
00:39:03,725 --> 00:39:05,386
Break dance!

270
00:39:43,131 --> 00:39:44,758
Tequila!

271
00:39:58,446 --> 00:40:00,437
Thanks a lot, dudes.

272
00:40:02,417 --> 00:40:04,282
I hope you find your bike.

273
00:40:33,996 --> 00:40:37,988
The customized bicycle was presented
to child star, Kevin Morton...

274
00:40:38,332 --> 00:40:42,166
...at Warner Brothers Studios
in Hollywood, California.

275
00:40:43,037 --> 00:40:44,504
Congratulations, Kevin.

276
00:40:44,839 --> 00:40:46,397
Thanks, Mr. Hawthorne.

277
00:40:46,474 --> 00:40:48,738
A bike like this is every boy's dream.

278
00:41:13,634 --> 00:41:15,261
Excuse me, sir.
Do you have a pass?

279
00:41:15,536 --> 00:41:17,868
Oh, no, I' sorry you can't
enter without a pass.

280
00:41:20,474 --> 00:41:23,807
So the fellow said, "What do you think
I have down here, a duck?"

281
00:41:30,017 --> 00:41:31,382
A duck!

282
00:41:52,273 --> 00:41:54,400
Where can I find Kevin Morton?

283
00:41:56,978 --> 00:41:58,070
I don't know.

284
00:41:58,879 --> 00:42:01,074
Do you know what stage
Kevin Morton is on?

285
00:42:01,882 --> 00:42:03,372
It's stage six.

286
00:42:09,423 --> 00:42:11,084
All right. I want to go once again.

287
00:42:26,907 --> 00:42:28,932
Hair standing by.

288
00:42:32,947 --> 00:42:36,383
What I want to do now,
is I want to do one more, faster paced.

289
00:42:36,584 --> 00:42:37,448
All right, Kevin?

290
00:42:37,518 --> 00:42:39,042
You know, I would love to...

291
00:42:39,120 --> 00:42:42,021
...except how can I
when she's so late on her cues?

292
00:42:42,957 --> 00:42:44,447
Just a minute!

293
00:42:47,995 --> 00:42:48,859
Please, Marion.

294
00:42:51,032 --> 00:42:53,796
I don't have to take that
from that little...

295
00:42:54,135 --> 00:42:56,126
Kid! He's just a kid.

296
00:42:56,270 --> 00:42:59,262
Even a kid can be courteous.
I'm going to quit.

297
00:42:59,807 --> 00:43:02,367
I swear it, I am going to quit!

298
00:43:03,677 --> 00:43:06,202
All right, Jerry. But I have had it!

299
00:43:09,316 --> 00:43:11,409
Well, is everything straightened out?

300
00:43:11,485 --> 00:43:12,816
We're ready when you are.

301
00:43:13,054 --> 00:43:15,887
Doesn't it look like I'm ready?!
I am always ready!

302
00:43:16,157 --> 00:43:20,150
I have been ready since first call!
I am ready!

303
00:43:20,694 --> 00:43:21,820
Roll!

304
00:43:22,496 --> 00:43:24,828
Quiet, please! This is a take!

305
00:43:27,568 --> 00:43:28,557
Action!

306
00:43:30,304 --> 00:43:31,999
Good-bye, Mother Superior.

307
00:43:32,273 --> 00:43:35,765
Good-bye, Rusty. And God bless you.

308
00:43:36,911 --> 00:43:41,007
Thank you Mother Superior,
I want the orphanage to have my bike.

309
00:43:41,348 --> 00:43:42,576
No, Rusty.

310
00:43:42,850 --> 00:43:46,513
You sold a lot of magazine subscriptions
to earn that bike.

311
00:43:46,854 --> 00:43:49,186
But I want to give.

312
00:43:49,790 --> 00:43:54,454
I've just received the two best parents
a boy could ever hope for.

313
00:43:54,895 --> 00:43:59,195
Rusty, you are an inspiration to us all.

314
00:43:59,567 --> 00:44:00,761
I'll say.

315
00:44:01,402 --> 00:44:04,565
I'm going to start
a paper route right now.

316
00:44:08,542 --> 00:44:10,134
Stop that nun!

317
00:44:17,885 --> 00:44:20,376
Remember me? Let's go!

318
00:46:48,269 --> 00:46:49,759
Merry Christmas!

319
00:48:58,876 --> 00:49:00,707
Geronimo!

320
00:49:10,020 --> 00:49:11,578
Radical!

321
00:49:42,719 --> 00:49:44,550
You can help me. Come on!

322
00:49:44,788 --> 00:49:46,278
Don't panic!

323
00:49:46,356 --> 00:49:48,347
No pushing, no shoving.

324
00:49:49,560 --> 00:49:53,394
Move in an orderly fashion
to the front exit.

325
00:50:03,240 --> 00:50:04,502
Stay!

326
00:50:04,741 --> 00:50:06,675
Listen up, everybody! Sit!

327
00:50:24,761 --> 00:50:25,557
It's okay.

328
00:50:37,107 --> 00:50:38,199
Go on! Run!

329
00:50:45,616 --> 00:50:48,278
Fast! Come on! Let's go!

330
00:51:38,368 --> 00:51:41,098
Son, are you all right?
Can you hear me?

331
00:51:41,438 --> 00:51:43,929
There's still a few more fish inside.

332
00:51:44,641 --> 00:51:45,938
This boy is a hero.

333
00:51:46,176 --> 00:51:48,167
This boy is under arrest.

334
00:52:05,329 --> 00:52:07,456
I can explain, Mr. Hawthorne.

335
00:52:07,965 --> 00:52:09,296
Call me "Terry."

336
00:52:12,502 --> 00:52:15,801
Warner Brothers thinks your story
would make a fantastic movie.

337
00:52:16,073 --> 00:52:18,405
My story. A movie?!

338
00:52:25,315 --> 00:52:26,247
My bike!

339
00:52:34,391 --> 00:52:35,483
Do we have a deal?

340
00:53:09,126 --> 00:53:11,356
Pee-wee, can I have your autograph?

341
00:53:17,367 --> 00:53:19,358
Here's your chili dog.

342
00:53:27,210 --> 00:53:30,543
Pee-wee! Over here. Look! Box seats!

343
00:53:32,749 --> 00:53:37,209
This is Bob, Luke, Skinny and Milton.
Boys, this is Pee-wee!

344
00:53:38,055 --> 00:53:39,613
Sno-cones.

345
00:53:40,057 --> 00:53:42,548
I never met a movie star.

346
00:53:43,894 --> 00:53:45,384
What did they pay you?

347
00:53:47,798 --> 00:53:49,459
Nice to meet you.

348
00:54:08,285 --> 00:54:10,310
Let's take a breather, Dottie.

349
00:54:10,554 --> 00:54:12,419
The X-1 needs to cool down.

350
00:54:14,424 --> 00:54:16,585
I'm a little overheated myself.

351
00:54:18,528 --> 00:54:20,428
Come over here, P.W.

352
00:55:01,638 --> 00:55:03,469
I must get to a phone.

353
00:55:13,150 --> 00:55:16,210
Great so far, Pee-wee.
Action packed.

354
00:55:16,653 --> 00:55:18,052
One soda.

355
00:55:18,989 --> 00:55:21,651
One foot-Iong!

356
00:55:29,065 --> 00:55:30,828
Good try, Pee-wee.

357
00:55:41,545 --> 00:55:45,504
Have you got any message for Room 104?
The name is Herman.

358
00:55:46,416 --> 00:55:47,906
P.W. Herman.

359
00:55:53,857 --> 00:55:56,519
No, nothing right now, Mr. Herman.

360
00:55:59,529 --> 00:56:01,019
I'll be in the bar.

361
00:56:07,204 --> 00:56:09,035
That's fantastic!

362
00:56:20,884 --> 00:56:22,044
Ditto.

363
00:56:22,385 --> 00:56:24,876
I brought you guys French fries!

364
00:56:35,232 --> 00:56:37,564
The big scene's coming up, guys!

365
00:56:47,244 --> 00:56:49,235
Paging Mr. Herman.

366
00:56:49,579 --> 00:56:53,640
Mr. Herman, you have a telephone call
at the front desk.

367
00:57:08,832 --> 00:57:10,424
Yes, I understand.

368
00:57:13,336 --> 00:57:14,826
That was the president.

369
00:57:15,005 --> 00:57:16,700
I must steal back the X-1...

370
00:57:16,773 --> 00:57:20,106
...before the Soviets find
the hidden microfilm inside.

371
00:57:20,844 --> 00:57:23,711
The future of the free world
is riding on this.

372
00:57:23,780 --> 00:57:27,272
-I'll go with you.
-No, it's too dangerous.

373
00:57:28,418 --> 00:57:31,285
I invented the X-1.
I'm going with you!

374
00:57:31,755 --> 00:57:33,188
All right, let's go.

375
00:57:34,958 --> 00:57:37,449
You are such a pushover.

376
00:57:38,762 --> 00:57:40,286
I know you are...

377
00:57:40,931 --> 00:57:42,364
...but what am I?

378
00:57:52,042 --> 00:57:53,873
Congratulations, Pee-wee!

379
00:57:55,011 --> 00:57:56,638
Hi, P.W.

380
00:57:57,647 --> 00:57:58,978
How's the X-1?

381
00:57:59,316 --> 00:58:02,308
It's cooled down. But I'm heated up.

382
00:58:02,986 --> 00:58:05,318
Where's my candy?

383
00:58:05,822 --> 00:58:07,153
I forgot.

384
00:58:11,895 --> 00:58:13,760
Pee-wee and I go way back.

385
00:58:13,830 --> 00:58:16,321
When did you become blood brothers?

386
00:58:16,666 --> 00:58:18,497
I don't remember the exact year.

387
00:58:18,668 --> 00:58:21,159
And you say you taught Pee-wee
to ride his bike?

388
00:58:21,871 --> 00:58:24,738
I remember the day I took off
his training wheels.

389
00:58:26,609 --> 00:58:28,167
This is the bike.

390
00:58:29,012 --> 00:58:30,843
How about a picture of me on it?

391
00:58:31,081 --> 00:58:32,412
I don't think that's a good idea.

392
00:58:32,749 --> 00:58:35,081
It's not your decision.

393
00:58:35,352 --> 00:58:39,686
If it wasn't for me, none of this
would have happened to you, right?

394
00:58:40,357 --> 00:58:42,018
Well, sort of.

395
00:58:42,359 --> 00:58:45,419
Then it's okay if I sit on it.
Right, Pee-wee?

396
00:58:47,864 --> 00:58:50,856
Come on, Pee-wee, everybody's waiting.

397
00:58:57,040 --> 00:58:58,405
Everyone, gather around.

398
00:58:58,508 --> 00:59:01,204
Let me show you some of
the more high-tech features.

399
00:59:18,495 --> 00:59:20,986
You don't want to get mixed up with me.

400
00:59:21,398 --> 00:59:23,866
I'm a Ioner, Dottie. A rebel.

401
00:59:30,407 --> 00:59:32,238
Come on, Dottie. Let's go.

402
00:59:33,176 --> 00:59:35,167
Don't you want to see
the rest of the movie?

403
00:59:35,245 --> 00:59:36,940
I don't have to see it, Dottie.

404
00:59:37,414 --> 00:59:51,276
I lived it.

405
00:59:51,661 --> 01:00:52,281
